R(6,41,'18–37','The degree/subscript of H_B in the requested Tate isomorphism is unsure.','Read the total degree and the underlined Construire/Conditions word before assigning an assertion.','The Hodge summand H^q(Ω^p) belongs in total degree p+q; the question-sheet context does not turn it into a theorem.','high','medium')
R(6,43,'71–99','Uncertain implication sign near the structures1 and2.','Distinguish implication from equivalence and retain the two-weight Hodge–Tate hypothesis.','Invariant reconstruction is valid conditionally; the universal converse is false for arbitrary semilinear representations.','high','low')
R(6,43,'102–103','Second diagonal entry of the displayed cocharacter matrix is unsure.','Determine whether it is t,1 or another expression from the ink.','The smallest algebraic subgroup depends on the actual weights, not merely the word groupe.','high','low')
R(6,44,'119–129','g(z) is written next to a Cauchy kernel and measure with no integral sign.','Possible omitted integral sign; retain literal diplomatic formula.','Cauchy representation and the following Fubini exchange require integration; scalar multiplication by an unspecified measure is not the same formula.','high','high')
R(6,46,'181–197','Lemma2 starts with a compact L but later uses C−K.','Either K=L or one of the letters is misread; inspect another witness.','Without identifying the compact set the holomorphy domain and supports are not a determinate hypothesis.','high','high')
R(6,48,'209–215','hypersingulières is expressly glossed sans points d’ordre p.','Keep p-rank zero unless ink changes the gloss; do not modernize the term.','The general Barsotti question is false for p-rank zero but positive for modern supersingular/all-slopes-one-half varieties.','high','high')
R(6,49,'223–225','unsure tte courbe in an assertion about E×F and two-dimensional moduli.','Possibly toute surface or toute variété of the preceding type.','A curve cannot be isomorphic to a product of two elliptic curves. The surface reconstruction is explicit and conditional.','high','medium')
R(6,49,'223–225','isogène is replaced by isomorphe.','Verify replacement direction and whether any extra condition was inserted.','The natural surface reading of the isomorphism assertion is false, as the explicit genus-two Jacobian shows. Mathematics cannot undo a clearly written author error.','high','medium')
R(6,50,'235–241','det theta and the revised Frobenius polynomial argument.','Possibly reduced norm/determinant in the quaternion algebra; determine the surviving wording and base field.','An ordinary matrix determinant and reduced norm are different notions. A central transcendental unit gives a valid reconstructed obstruction without resolving the ink.','high','medium')
R(6,53,'254–286','Two extension symbols are both transcribed xi_0.','Distinguish the given special-fibre extension from a chosen trivial extension/origin.','The deformation space is intrinsically a torsor until an origin is fixed; confusing the symbols changes the claimed canonical group structure.','high','medium')
R(6,54,'301–318','The compact Tate-lifting parenthesis is unsure.','Read the exact connected/multiplicative and lifting qualifications.','Ordinary Serre–Tate theory does not automatically prove the stated torsor for every connected N_0.','high','low')
R(6,56,'365–383','Cancelled NB about flatness has obscured wording.','Determine the exact negation and the full extent of cancellation.','The dimension argument on057 invokes flatness; a cancelled doubt cannot be silently promoted to a proved mixed-characteristic statement.','high','low')
R(6,57,'387–404','Connective preceding prime-to-p polarization smoothness is unsure.','Check implication direction and the inserted restriction to ordinary varieties.','The local-ring computation uses ordinary Serre–Tate coordinates; deleting that restriction would assert a false general moduli statement.','high','medium')
R(6,59,'412–472','Lemma1 says à gauche; Lemma2(c) says à droite.','Preserve both until the action on the two Ext variables is identified.','F[a]=[a^p]F is noncommutative over F_p[t]; a side swap changes the module statement.','high','high')
R(6,59,'425–444','The map in a_2 is not explicitly identified.','Read the arrow and its source/target before interpreting a vanishing or restriction statement.','The four-part induction uses different Witt and additive maps; replacing one by the expected V would fill a gap.','high','low')
R(6,59,'425–472','Crowded hypothesis on H being finite and locally free.','Determine which alternatives and all subsequent subparts the insertion qualifies.','A statement about G_a and a finite locally free subgroup need not hold for an arbitrary additive subgroup sheaf.','high','medium')
R(6,60,'487–531','Hom smoothness paragraph, its proof and §5 relations are struck through.','Verify extent of the deletion while keeping the live part(b) separate.','The live sheaf-Ext claim and the withdrawn Hom claim have different statuses; cancellation is not merely punctuation.','high','high')
R(6,62,'597–615','RHom(G,O) is identified with a tensor expression without an evident shift.','Check for a missing cohomological shift and for Cartier versus ordinary dual notation.','For G=Z/p and O=F_p, RHom has degrees0,1 while derived tensor has degrees−1,0; tensor[-1] repairs the cohomological grading.','high','high')
R(6,63,'655–682','Direction of the Hom-vanishing claim and cotangent/Hom notation.','Check the direction of the Hom arguments and any dual symbol.','Maps from a multiplicative group to an étale group and maps in the other direction are different functors; the argument depends on the actual direction.','high','medium')
R(6,65,'688–746','The Frobenius map may be semilinear rather than an O-linear endomorphism.','Read F^*M→M or the equivalent semilinear wording.','Fixed vectors classify local systems only with the linearized Frobenius isomorphism; ordinary linear automorphisms are a different problem.','high','medium')
R(6,66,'770–792','Uncertain Witt-category symbols at the end of the page.','Read the completion, level and F/V conventions instead of supplying a familiar modern category.','No exact equivalence can be evaluated until these objects and morphisms are fixed.','high','low')
R(7,3,'833–868','Several infinitesimal-neighbourhood indices and arrows are cramped.','Check the n+1-fold product convention and inverse transition direction.','The Čech degree n has n+1 factors; confusing neighbourhood order with cosimplicial degree shifts all face maps.','high','medium')
R(7,4,'870–910','The tensor-product formula suppresses which O_X actions are used.','Determine the two extreme projections and the restricted scalar action.','Principal parts carries two O_X actions; the later differential-operator functoriality depends on their choice.','high','medium')
R(7,7,'930–944','The augmentation/shifted cosimplicial symbols are revised.','Check the degree-zero augmentation and the indexing shift.','A contracted augmented complex and its unaugmented truncation have different H^0.','high','medium')
R(7,8,'946–955','Restricted pro-category and abelianness are questioned.','Read whether the category is all pro-modules or an Artin–Rees subcategory.','The former being abelian does not answer closure/exactness in the latter.','high','medium')
R(7,13,'1027–1057','An ell-like operator precedes Q^0 in the spectral-sequence expressions.','Determine whether it is a limit, derived operation or a separately defined symbol.','A spectral-sequence target cannot be fixed by erasing this operator; lim and derived lim need not agree.','high','low')
R(7,14,'1059–1075','The characteristic-zero hypothesis occurs in the formal Poincaré argument.','Check that the base is a Q-scheme, not merely a characteristic-zero domain.','The contracting homotopy divides by positive integers; Z_p or Z has characteristic zero but does not allow those divisions.','high','high')
R(7,15,'1084–1096','An ell-like prefix is cancelled before Q^0 in one display.','Keep live and deleted expressions distinct and inspect the grading of the surviving map.','The direction is from stratification cohomology to de Rham cohomology; altering the operator or reversing the arrow changes the proposed comparison.','high','medium')
