R(7,23,'1246–1253','H^0_dR is written as literal pth powers without a repeated perfectness condition.','Check whether the earlier perfect-field hypothesis applies; otherwise use relative Frobenius only as a reconstruction.','Over F_p(u), constants killed by d are not all literal pth powers.','high','high')
R(7,24,'1269–1273','The singularity is abbreviated rebr. ordinaire.','Verify whether it means an ordinary cusp and whether any different singularity or complex is specified.','For y²=x³ over C, the full Kähler complex has H^1=0, so the natural cusp reading gives an invalid example. This may be an author error rather than a transcription error.','high','medium')
R(7,26,'1309–1316','A revised/cancelled passage concerns Hodge-type or algebraic-cycle statements.','Read the cancellation and the precise group before making a conjecture from it.','A cancelled cycle assertion must not be imported as a live Hodge conjecture or as part of the singular comparison.','high','low')
