R(7,40,'1549–1575','The primitive criterion only states a valuation tail tending to infinity.','Determine whether the ambient calculation is over W or K=W[1/p].','Over W the coefficientwise inequality v_p(a_n)≥v_p(n+1) is also needed; t^(p−1)dt is a polynomial counterexample to a tail-only integral criterion.','high','high')
R(7,41,'1577–1590','|a_n|=O(1)rho^n with rho>1.','Possibly rho^(−n), or 0<rho<1 with the written positive exponent.','The literal bound permits a_n=1 and restricted subexponential coefficients; it does not express overconvergence. The original doubts report no visible minus, so an author slip remains possible.','high','high')
